 "why": "A pin identifies a recipe by a fingerprint over its shape so it survives a redump renumbering every id. When the pack changes the recipe the fingerprint stops matching and the pin falls back to its CATEGORY, which is the path this pins the port to -- the solver keeps its own ranking among whatever the category permits rather than being handed a choice made by dump order. The `pinned` badge on the node is part of the contract: a choice you cannot see is a choice you cannot audit."
